-- The exhibit for the DMN exporter (Track D1 of the Lexipedia-superset
-- programme). Modelled on the decision logic of Regulation Crowdfunding that
-- the Lexipedia page draws as BPMN *gateways* -- which is the category error
-- the programme is about: eligibility and the investor limit are decisions, and
-- a decision belongs in a decision table.
--
-- Five decisions, deliberately of five different shapes, so the goldens show
-- every outcome the exporter has -- and most of the fidelity notes it can emit
-- -- at once:
--
--   * `is accredited investor`        U hit policy over a CONSIDER, OTHERWISE as
--                                     the <defaultOutputEntry>; constant
--                                     outputs, so NOTHING is lost;
--   * `combined resources`            not a guarded chain, so a
--                                     <literalExpression>   [D-LITERALEXPR];
--   * `annual limit basis`            a conditional whose arms are its own
--                                     comparison's operands: that is `min`, not
--                                     a decision, and is lifted;
--   * `financial statements required` a WHERE-wrapped chain of ELSE-IFs: peeled,
--                                     inlined and flattened into four sibling
--                                     rules              [D-INLINEDLOCAL];
--   * `investor limit`                F hit policy over overlapping guards, with
--                                     a lifted floor and a computed output
--                                     [D-LIFTEDTHRESHOLD, D-COMPUTEDOUTPUT,
--                                     D-ORDERDEPENDENT].
--
-- Figures are illustrative. The point of the exhibit is the SHAPE, not the
-- currency of the numbers.
--
-- The heading below is load-bearing: `l4 export --to=dmn` with no
-- `--model-name` takes the <definitions> name from a module's outermost
-- section, so the model is named once, here, by the file that is the model.

§ `Regulation Crowdfunding`

ASSUME `annual income` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `net worth` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `offering amount` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `first-time issuer` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Investor Class`
  IS ONE OF
    `accredited`
    `retail`
    `institutional`

ASSUME `class` IS A `Investor Class`

-- A CONSIDER over distinct nullary constructors: the guards cannot both hold,
-- so the table is honestly Unique and OTHERWISE becomes the default output.
-- FEEL has no sum types, so the constructors serialise as strings. Constant
-- outputs plus a single-hit policy means this table is INSIDE the fragment
-- DMN's own analysis is defined over, and the report says nothing about it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is accredited investor` IF
  CONSIDER `class`
  WHEN `accredited`    THEN TRUE
  WHEN `institutional` THEN TRUE
  OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Not a guarded chain: plain arithmetic. DMN's own answer for logic with no
-- table shape is a boxed literal expression, and the fidelity report says so
-- rather than the exporter quietly dropping the decision.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`combined resources` MEANS
  `annual income` PLUS `net worth`

-- 17 CFR 227.100(a)(2) says "the LESSER of". The L4 spells that longhand, but
-- both arms are exactly the two operands of the guard, so it is `min` -- and
-- expanding it into a two-row table would manufacture cases the regulation does
-- not have. Lifted to FEEL's own min(). No threshold note: two symmetric
-- computed quantities are arithmetic, not policy.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`annual limit basis` MEANS
  IF `annual income` AT MOST `net worth` THEN `annual income` ELSE `net worth`

-- Successively higher thresholds, each ELSE-IF introducing a condition the one
-- above did not. THIS one is a real decision and does flatten -- into four
-- sibling rules, under First. Note also that the WHERE-local `aggregate` has to
-- be peeled and inlined before the chain is visible to the normaliser at all.
GIVETH A STRING
`financial statements required` MEANS
  IF   `aggregate` AT MOST 107000
  THEN "certified by the principal executive officer"
  ELSE IF   `aggregate` AT MOST 535000
       THEN "reviewed by an independent public accountant"
       ELSE IF   `first-time issuer relief applies`
            THEN "reviewed by an independent public accountant"
            ELSE "audited by an independent public accountant"
  WHERE
  `aggregate` MEANS `offering amount`
  `first-time issuer relief applies` MEANS
    `first-time issuer` AND `aggregate` AT MOST 1070000

-- Overlapping numeric thresholds: first match wins, so the hit policy is F and
-- no rule restates that an earlier one did not fire. The second output carries a
-- lifted $2,500 floor -- correct, because 227.100(a)(2)(i) says "The greater of
-- $2,500, or ..." -- and the report names it, because a compliance reader can no
-- longer point at the floor as a row of the table. The last output is computed,
-- which is legal DMN 8.2.9 and outside the fragment DMN's analysis covers.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`investor limit` MEANS
  BRANCH
    IF `is accredited investor` THEN 100000000
    IF `annual limit basis` LESS THAN 124000
      THEN IF 2500 AT LEAST `annual limit basis` THEN 2500 ELSE `annual limit basis`
    OTHERWISE `annual limit basis` * 10 / 100
